{"description":"Before an agent runs a recon tool, it must confirm the target domain is owned by the operator or explicitly authorised (bug-bounty scope, pentest engagement, own assets), per .kiro/steering/ethics-and-safety.md. If authorisation is unclear, the tool call must not proceed.","enabled":true,"name":"Scope guard before recon","then":{"prompt":"A recon tool from the sublist3r-reborn MCP server is about to run. Before allowing it: (1) identify the target domain in the tool arguments; (2) check the conversation and working notes for the operator's authorisation basis for that domain (they own it, it is in scope of a bug-bounty program, or it is a contracted pentest target); (3) state the domain and the authorisation basis in your reply. If no authorisation basis is established, do NOT proceed with the tool call — stop and ask the operator first. This implements the authorised-targets rule in .kiro/steering/ethics-and-safety.md.","type":"askAgent"},"version":"1","when":{"matcher":"enumerate_subdomains|check_takeover|resolve_records","type":"preToolUse"}}